# virtualenv
.venv/
# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
# large downloaded open datasets (regenerate via `python -m tmesim.cli acquire`)
# NOTE the trailing `*`: `data_cache/` excludes the DIRECTORY, so git never
# descends into it and a later `!data_cache/x/` cannot re-include anything.
# Excluding the CONTENTS instead is what makes the exceptions below work.
data_cache/*
#
# EXCEPT the hand-extracted anchor tables. The rule above is justified by
# "regenerate via acquire" -- these two cannot be. They were pulled out of
# publisher PDFs and six open-access papers by hand, carry per-value
# provenance, and record which rows are model-derived rather than measured.
# Re-deriving them means redoing the extraction and re-making every judgement
# call in it.
#
# They are also EVIDENCE. results/transport_anchor_prereg.md fixes a criterion
# against data_cache/brain_slice/, and results/brain_slice_anchor.md publishes
# a FAIL scored on it. A published result whose dataset is untracked is a
# result nobody can check -- which is the defect this project keeps finding in
# itself. 96 KB total; the size argument does not apply.
!data_cache/pruijn2008/
!data_cache/pruijn2008/**
!data_cache/brain_slice/
!data_cache/brain_slice/**
# per-regime experiment output dirs (keep the top-level result artifacts)
results/regime_pp*/
results/tl_pp*/
# tmesim Studio local run history + binary payloads (regenerated by re-running)
app/runs/
# tmesim Studio local projects/studies (ids into app/runs/, not results)
app/projects/
# tmesim Studio generated therapy reports (assembled from app/runs/, regenerable)
app/reports/
# tmesim Studio "bring your own compound" store. USER DATA: an operator's own
# SMILES and their own IC50s -- an unpublished compound series is exactly the
# thing that must not be committed. Only the inputs are ever written here (every
# compiled number is recomputed on read); see results/bring_your_own_compound.md.
app/compounds/

# Private build store for the static export (regenerate: scripts/studio_export/export_studio_runs.py)
results/export_runs/

# Runtime upload directory for TPL "drug ... from file" (contents are user data)
app/uploads/*
!app/uploads/.gitkeep

# Regenerable stage cache for the immune-sink sweep (delete to force recompute)
results/immune_sink_impact_cache.pkl

# Local browser-verification screenshots (not build output, not for the repo)
.export-drive/

# Agent worktrees and session scratch — never part of the repo.
.claude/

# Browser profiles used for headless UI verification. NEVER commit one.
#
# This is here because it already happened: `results/fprof/` -- a full Chrome
# profile, 523 files and 110 MB including Cookies, Login Data, Web Data and
# History -- was committed in 8d703d3 and pushed. It is referenced by no code.
# A profile directory is not an artifact; it is a credential store that happens
# to live in a folder, and a headless run will silently create one wherever it
# is pointed. Point it at the scratchpad, never inside the repo.
#
# NOTE: this pattern stops FUTURE commits only. Git keeps tracking files it
# already tracks, so `results/fprof/` remains in the working tree and in
# history until it is explicitly removed -- see results/security_audit.md (C3).
results/fprof/
results/*profile/
*/Default/Login Data
*/Default/Cookies
